{{wp|North (disambiguation)|north}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|north}}, from {{inh|en|ang|norþ}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*norþr}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*nurþrą}}, ultimately, these may derive from either: (a) {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₁ner-||inner, under}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*h₁en||in}}; (b) alternatively from a {{der|en|ine-pro|*ner-||left, below}}, as north is to the left when one faces the rising sun.

Cognate with various Germanic counterparts such as {{cog|nl|noord}}, {{cog|fy|noard}}, {{cog|de|Nord}}, {{cog|da|-}} and {{cog|no|nord}}; also with {{cog|el|νέρτερος||infernal, lower}}.

